  "structure": {
    "block_count": 26,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Dealing With a Squirmy Baby",
        "text_sha256": "58591a4010cb69f890e1aef7a7b896da7a59ac49ef826f2e0f45230631e43f09",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For someone who’s just discovering her mobility, it’s no fun taking life sitting down…or lying down for a diaper change . Luckily, older babies may be stubbornly squirmy, but they’re still easily distracted.",
        "text_sha256": "de9871c1b38b04bb659881521c8bd9ade6c5ddccfba928a2ffd92d38631467f4",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Distract your baby. So keep the distractions coming. In the tub, sing a special, silly bath-time song, blow bubbles for baby to pop, make a splash (if she’s game, of course), fill and empty cups, float and sink ships, or dunk the dolly.",
        "text_sha256": "5bc0974493129184a218fd00a6194a0cd8adf16854d7ffa307719bff3dca5b77",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Work fast. Work fast, too — unless your little one’s really grimy, a few quick swipes with a washcloth should get the job done with a minimum of wriggling. The less attention paid to the wriggling, by the way, the better — smiles or scolding will both reinforce the behavior you’re trying to discourage. Same holds for babies who won’t hold still for diaper changes.",
        "text_sha256": "5769bce7f2b3722ccd5abd6fd19f353997f8e33ead4fc52e497e3651e0a92b82",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Keep your baby entertained. A special stash of just-for-diaper-changes toys (rotate them so baby doesn’t get bored) may elicit a few moments of cooperation, as may a giggly round of “stinky feet” or a silly diaper ditty.",
        "text_sha256": "d73184786289c5b4421a1bb89c7c6c26c1e775c44a9743e3f1a4ec37336e6dd9",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Change locations. You can also try a change of place. If your baby’s already standing up — try changing her where she stands. If the changing table has become the scene of too many struggles, move to a neutral location, like the family room floor. Wherever you’re changing, make sure you’ve gathered up all of your supplies ahead of time so you’ll be able to work faster.",
        "text_sha256": "046b4a0c0da7a9c69b01e25b4cfb077cc26efdc8579b4e1cdd626ab390c59154",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Never leave your baby alone. And of course, since squirmy babies can squirm into a whole lot of trouble fast, never leave your baby’s side while she’s on a changing table or in the tub — not even for a moment.",
        "text_sha256": "4d076ef03e6e226497c034eef854b99e1ce4c737f103488972a97783eb5743c6",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Go to Your Baby's Age",
        "text_sha256": "05a2c9b32af919d9a0a87b2762079ec33dc5246c16eaee9f0c85c8e3a83fe2ad",
        "word_count": 5
      },
